lse,"num_turns":1,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"**Normal period:** Under Rule 485(a)(2), a post-effective amendment adding a new series to an existing trust normally becomes effective **75 days after filing**, unless the SEC accelerates or the registrant delays it. Most other 485(a) amendments take **60 days** under 485(a)(1).\n\n**Not a launch guarantee:**\n- SEC staff comments may require changes or a delay.\n- Final terms usually go in a Rule 485(b) filing, and the date can be pushed back under 485(a)(3)/(b)(1)(iii).\n- Launch also needs board approvals and Form 8-A. It also needs exchange listing under generic listing standards (for Rule 6c-11 ETFs) or a Rule 19b-4 filing.\n- Operational needs include CUSIP, seed capital, authorized participants, custody, index licensing and service-provider contracts.\n\n**New trust:** It files Form N-8A and an initial N-1A under Securities Act §8(a), so no 485 timeline applies. Effectiveness is nominally 20 days, but filers almost always add a Rule 473 delaying amendment. Timing then depends on SEC review and acceleration, which often takes months.","ttft_ms":7462,"type":"result","duration_ms":10091,"uuid":"70da5950-a686-4137-8b5a-6017d42ba71c","ttft_stream_ms":1546,"time_to_request_ms":54,"first_content_frame_ms":1547,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
